the attack happened as israel celebrated  74 years of independence this time in  aladd an ultra-orthodox city in the  centre of the country ilad is very close  to the occupied west bank we do not  have full indication  if it's a one terrorist or more we are  conducting a  chase after him  we have a helicopter with us and we are  setting roadblocks in order to catch him  residents came out to protest in the  aftermath it's the latest in a series of  attacks carried out by individuals  across israel which has left at least 14  israelis dead a spokesperson for hamas  reacted by saying these attacks were the  result of israel's occupation of  palestinians u.n middle east envoy  torvenisland tweeted saying he was  appalled by the attack and that it was  deplorable that hamas and others  continue to glorify and encourage such  acts  israeli media replayed a clip from hamas  leader in gaza yahya sinwa who in a  fiery speech last week called on  palestinians to protect the al-aqsa  mosque compound referring to the recent  escalations at the site by the entry of  jewish religious ultranationalists and  encouraging individual attacks  defence minister benny ganz met with the  military chief of staff and the israeli  prime minister nathalie bennett was  being updated on the situation the  border crossings from gaza and the  occupied west bank had been closed since  tuesday afternoon due to memorial day  and independence day in what is standard  procedure doing events like these in  israel the west bank closure has now  been extended until sunday as a result  of this attack stephanie decker  al-jazeera west jerusalem
 

